## Why Phone Apps Have Better D-Pad Feel Than Physical Remotes

This is a subtle but real advantage of using a phone-based remote over a physical remote:

### 1. Haptic Feedback

Physical D-pad buttons give tactile feedback through the click of a button press. Phone remote apps can simulate this with **haptic vibration** — a tiny, precise buzz with each button tap. Many users find this more satisfying and responsive than a mushy physical button.

### 2. Larger Buttons

Physical remotes are small. The D-pad is typically less than 3cm in diameter. On a phone screen, the D-pad can be rendered as large as the screen allows. Bigger buttons mean fewer accidental presses in the wrong direction — especially useful when watching in the dark.

### 3. Customizable Layout

With a phone app, the D-pad size and position can be adjusted. Can't do that with a physical remote.

### 4. Backlit and Always-Visible

Phone screens are always lit, making buttons visible in a dark room. Physical remotes require backlighting (a premium feature) or squinting in the dark.

