## Pro Tips for D-Pad Navigation on Android TV

**Tip 1: Long-press Back to exit deep menus quickly**
In some apps, you've gone three or four screens deep. Long-pressing Back on some Android TV builds exits all the way to the app's home screen in one action.

**Tip 2: Use the Home button as a reset**
If you're lost in a menu or an app froze your navigation, pressing Home always gets you back to the TV's home screen. It's your safety net.

**Tip 3: Press Center during video playback to show controls**
Most video apps hide their playback controls overlay. A single Center press reveals the progress bar, title, and control buttons. Another press hides them again.

**Tip 4: Navigate text fields carefully**
When a text input field has focus, Left/Right arrow presses move the cursor within the text. Pressing Back exits the text field. Use the app's keyboard icon to bring up the full keyboard for faster input.

**Tip 5: App-specific menus are usually at the top**
In most Android TV apps, navigation tabs and menus are at the top of the screen. Pressing Up from the main content area usually takes you to the app's navigation bar.

